Key Points:

Regular users can only view the employee list (EmployeeListView doesn't have UserIsAdminMixin)

Admin users (superusers) can create, update, delete employees and calculate salaries

The authentication is handled by Django's built-in auth system

Authorization is handled through the UserIsAdminMixin

To enhance security, you might want to:

Add login rate limiting

Implement password complexity requirements

Use Django's messages framework for better user feedback

Add logging for admin actions

Example of enhanced security:

from django.contrib.auth.mixins import LoginRequiredMixin

class EmployeeListView(LoginRequiredMixin, ListView):
    # This ensures even the list view requires login
    model = Employee
    template_name = 'employees_list.html'
    context_object_name = 'employees'

